It's not an axiom it is a sentence.

Let's look about the truth value of that sentence:

If we make slings work like physics (the real world) describe they 
should work it doesn't matter if you are basing it on physics or 
scriptures of mumbo jumbo the great. It's half a dozen other and six of 
the other, but it would make the slings work better and as real slings do.

If we make slings better but a way that is different of the real world 
slins we are confusing players. The assumption of a player is that 
mundane items work like mundane items work. Magical items work against 
intuition, but a sling is not a magical item. That's one of the reasons 
why I haven't written anything how enchantment (negative or positive) 
should affect how a sling works.

So I say that the sentence:

The only rationale to make slings work better is that they do not work 
like real slings do.

is true.

